    "summary": "Persian mullah with a bazaar prostitute; single-page painting on an album folio. An open book lies on the mullah&#039;s lap, as he looks at the ambivalent lady smoking from a water pipe. The prostitute wears long robes that cover both her hair and body, with painted fingers and feet. She smokes the pipe in one hand, while holding a small cup in the other. Inscribed. Album contains 44 paintings and drawings, mostly of Persian costumes and animals with some drawings by Kaempfer.\r\nInk and opaque watercolour on paper. Album is bound in brown leather with gold gilt  decoration. Inside covers have marbled paper.",
